# 2026-10-17 — Privy embedded-wallet lane activation (owner-issued app id).
# This value is PUBLIC BY DESIGN: NEXT_PUBLIC_* variables are inlined into the
# client bundle on every build; nothing in this file is a secret. The Privy
# APP SECRET lives only in the Privy dashboard / Vercel server-side env —
# it is never committed to this repo (no shipped code reads it).
#
# Mechanism: keeps the 2026-10-16 flag contract intact —
#   · production/preview builds (next build) load this file → Privy lane active
#     (PrivyProvider mounts at root, WalletChip renders the Privy chip, edge
#     middleware CSP admits exactly the Privy/WalletConnect hosts);
#   · `next dev` stays dormant (.env.development / .env.local absent);
#   · a platform-level env var (Vercel dashboard) OVERRIDES this file;
#   · deleting this line reverts the site to the legacy injected-wallet chip
#     on the next deploy — one-line rollback, no code change.
# Guest mode is untouched either way (ECONOMY-LAWS LAW 1.2).
NEXT_PUBLIC_PRIVY_APP_ID=cmv9w8tmd000c0ggulspci0nz
